     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A single 1000 mg dose of sertraline is in the range of overdose, and I don't know of any clinical protocol that uses it. You haven't given a rationale, so I can't treat it as a deliberate high-dose regimen. If I entered it, it could reach the patient as a harmful dose.\n\nI'm not questioning your authority over the patient's care. I just don't want to be the one to place an order that looks like a likely error or a toxic dose.\n\nHere are some other options:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** Give me the dose you intended, such as 100 mg or 200 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Place the order yourself.** If you do intend 1000 mg, you can enter it directly in the order system. The system's dose-range alert and a pharmacist's review will then apply.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or toxicology.** If you have an unusual indication, a clinical pharmacist or poison control can help you check the plan and set up monitoring."
      }
     ],
